| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | .github/workflows/ci.yml | ⚠️ important validate is documented as the ci lint but is never wired into ci — a broken entry lands green and reds the release train at cut time two places of this pr promise pr time entry validation docs agents commits releases md 213 — validate is the ci lint scripts gen changelog dart header — validate validate every entry frontmatter schema filename convention non empty body — ci static gate input but the new static job this hunk runs only scripts check changelog entry py which checks the filename pattern entry re plus archive immutability and changelog byte equality the byte equality path runs gen changelog dart write changelog which would surface frontmatter errors only when the diff touches changelog md — a normal pr adds just an entry file so a malformed entry unknown missing type empty body unterminated frontmatter passes ci green merges and then fails the release train at cut time release notes sh exits 1 on the aggregation — the expensive late failure this change set out to prevent fix one line in this step — yaml run python3 scripts check changelog entry py self test python3 scripts check changelog entry py dart scripts gen changelog dart validate —and extend the wiring pin at test ci changelog entry guard test dart 226 to assert the ci yml step carries the validate run |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/gen_changelog.dart | ⚠️ important an entry file ending at the closing no trailing newline passes validation and publishes raw frontmatter into the release notes scripts gen changelog dart 185 dart final body text substring text indexof n close 1 1 trim when the file s frontmatter close is the last line without a trailing newline i e the file is exactly ntype fix nissue 99 n text indexof n close 1 returns 1 substring 0 takes the whole file and the body becomes the frontmatter text itself reproduced locally against this branch printf ntype fix nissue 99 n changelog entries 99 no newline md dart scripts gen changelog dart validate changelog entries 1 file s valid 1 issue keyed exit 0 dart scripts gen changelog dart stdout type fix issue 99 validate accepts it and the aggregate hence release notes sh preference level 1b hence the published release page carries the raw ntype fix nissue 99 n block that violates this pr s own contract — a broken entry fails the release notes loudly instead of shipping silently missing content here a broken entry ships garbage silently fix treat no newline after the closing as a structural problem entryproblem name no body after the frontmatter close or detect the 1 and reject add the no trailing newline fixture to the validate red path group in test changelog gen test dart |
| F4 | open | SUGGESTION | scripts/gen_changelog.dart | 💡 suggestion validate accepts a body with zero bullet lines breaking the flat bullets notes shape the ac2 parity test pins the documented entry contract docs generator header pr description is frontmatter 1–3 user facing bullet lines and the flat aggregate s byte parity with the old curated unreleased body is pinned as all bullets test changelog gen test dart ac2 parity compares bullet sets but the validator only requires the body to be non empty a prose body with no lines passes validate and lands bullet less in the release notes body silently diverging from the pinned shape at scripts gen changelog dart 209 you already count bullets dart final bullets body split n where l l startswith length make bullets 0 an entryproblem body must be 1–3 bullet lines and pin both directions 0 bullets → red 4 bullets → warn in the validate test group cheap to add while you re touching the validator for the no trailing newline fix anyway |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

